<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves down to $1.728 bln on Oct 25.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves down to $1.728 bln on Oct 25.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.728 billion on October 25, down $89 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In the previous week to October 18, international reserves grew $24 million.</p>
<p>Central Bank did not give an explication for the growth of reserves.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
